1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,900
The record says: the records agree. What actually happened: eight of twelve joins compare a record with its own copy.

2
00:00:03,900 --> 00:00:10,800
Three failures at Store 014 in June. Two of its records, joined, showed each within hours: 3, 4.5 and 14.

3
00:00:10,800 --> 00:00:17,700
Join June’s records two at a time. Eight joins agree on every row, because one record is written from the other.

4
00:00:17,700 --> 00:00:24,600
Four joins sometimes disagree. On each, one side looks at the world, and each of June’s failures sits on one of them.

5
00:00:24,600 --> 00:00:31,500
The KPIs read copies. And no record looked at what was on a pallet.

6
00:00:31,500 --> 00:00:38,900
Tuesday, 8 pm: a silence at the store, followed to a short slot in the warehouse. The wrong line, named 61 hours before the count.

7
00:00:38,900 --> 00:00:45,300
Give the agent the map: 3 of 21 questions right with the schema, 21 of 21 with domain layers.

8
00:00:45,300 --> 00:00:50,300
Every record was right about what it saw. Join the ones that look at the world.
